  "history_summaries": [
    "Repair round 1: fixed setup_error for process0_progress_l1_to_cs (and symmetrical process1_progress_l1_to_cs). Root cause: io_select fairness constraint missing — environment could permanently select one process, starving the other (CEX showed io_select=1 forever, self stuck at 1, process 0 frozen at L2). Added assume(selectStableCnt < 4.U) that constrains io_select to change at least every 4 cycles using a stability counter (selectPrev/selectStableCnt). This ensures both processes get scheduled regularly, allowing Dekker's mutual-exclusion handshake to complete within the 50-cycle bound. Both failing liveness properties are addressed by this single environment constraint. Assertion labels preserved unchanged.",
    "Repair round 2: fixed setup_error for process0_progress_l1_to_cs and process1_progress_l1_to_cs. Root cause: io_pause fairness constraint missing — the environment could hold io.pause high for 18 consecutive cycles, stalling process 1 in L5 (critical section) and delaying c(1)=true (waiting at L4), which cascades to process 0 needing 52 cycles instead of the 50-cycle bound. Added assume(pauseStableCnt < 5.U) that constrains io_pause to change at least every 5 cycles using a stability counter (pausePrev/pauseStableCnt). This prevents unbounded stalling at L0 (idle entry) and L5 (CS exit), ensuring both processes can make timely progress to stay within the 50-cycle bound. The pause fairness constraint is structurally identical to the existing select fairness constraint. Both failing liveness properties are addressed by this single environment constraint. Assertion labels preserved unchanged (process0_progress_l1_to_cs, process1_progress_l1_to_cs).",
    "Repair round 3: fixed DUT bug for process0_progress_l1_to_cs and process1_progress_l1_to_cs. Root cause: the original state machine used `switch(pc(self))` which evaluated only ONE process per cycle (the one selected by `self`), serializing two independent concurrent processes. This caused artificial delays — a process at L2 could only check c(~self) when self selected it, and a process at L5 could only exit when self selected it AND !io.pause. The waveform confirmed process 0 spent 51 cycles oscillating L2↔L3 because self was often selecting process 1, missing windows where c(1)=1. Fix: replace `switch(pc(self))` with `for (i <- 0 until 2) { switch(pc(i)) { ... } }` so both processes evaluate their state machines independently each cycle, communicating through shared c() and turn registers as true concurrent Dekker execution requires. All assertion labels preserved unchanged (process0_progress_l1_to_cs, process1_progress_l1_to_cs)."
  ],
